    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0992" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5812A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-28T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                                1928—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. The Department handed the Swedish Minister today a draft of a proposed treaty
                    of arbitration between the United States and Sweden. The provisions of the draft
                    operate to extend the policy of arbitration enunciated in the Convention signed
                    at Washington on June 24, 1924.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d748-f1"/> which expires on
                    March 18, 1929. The language of the draft is identical in effect with that of
                    the Arbitration Treaty recently signed with France<anchor n="2" xml:id="d748-f2"
                    /> and with the draft arbitration treaties already submitted to other
                    governments in the general program for the extension of these principles. The
                    text of the proposed treaty will be forwarded in the next pouch.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d748-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
